     <QuerySet [<Choice: The sky>]>
 
+The ``queryset`` can also be :ref:`sliced <limiting-querysets>`, in which case
+the slice is applied to the related objects of each instance separately, e.g.
+to fetch the three most voted choices of each question:
+
+    >>> top_choices = Choice.objects.order_by('-votes')[:3]
+    >>> prefetch = Prefetch('choice_set', queryset=top_choices, to_attr='top_choices')
+    >>> Question.objects.prefetch_related(prefetch).get().top_choices
+    [<Choice: The sky>, <Choice: Not much>, <Choice: Just hacking again>]
+
+Prefetching from a sliced queryset is only supported on database backends that
+support :ref:`window functions <window-functions>`.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 4.2
+
+    Support for sliced querysets was added.
+
 The ``to_attr`` argument sets the result of the prefetch operation to a custom
 attribute:
 
